PianoA830 is the Adreno830 A830 kernel GPU driver (OnePlus 13T lineage) as a k27 native kext for piano, with piano's own board glue
(board/, BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). What it takes from other work, and from where:

Adreno830 (github.com/Shad0w23333/Adreno830; local unixnu-research/Adreno830), main 1a1321056ffc5428ae925f4680093718b46ca7c2
(unixnu.lock pin."Adreno830"), MIT (adreno830/LICENSE, sha256 16fbc0170994a48f60938d9f0d992d3bad113383cf90882f75c206e079c2a2dc).
  Copied into adreno830/: every file of the repository except docs/ and AGENTS.md (the design documents stay upstream; read them
  there), 159 files unchanged (sha256 equal to the originals). Hardware-proven on the 13T: S0-S10 and a GPU-composited desktop under
  iPadOS 17.7.11 (gpu-native-plan.md section 2). Changed, every change marked "UniXNU-piano" in a comment and compiled only with
  -DADRENO830_MACOS (the host tests build without it, so they test the upstream code paths):
    Adreno830Start.cpp      215e565650d176cd28c2e11e79e098195474add04ea5ae054b15e9eaa4ff0b0f -> f14a4ec706aca0a9742d8409ee3c75a526fb7747b8b09ae5cf21930bc0cb49a1
      S9 publishMetal without the iPadOS-only staged IOAcceleratorES (no IOGPUFamily load, no static class initializer, no
      g_kernel_kmod_info): prepare/commit report steps 4/5; the macOS accelerator is the kext's AGXAccelerator personality on the
      NativeAdrenoGpuPublished service native_adreno_publish registers. The 128 KiB cmd-db snapshot on the heap (allocated once by
      adreno830_start): the k27 collection's largest __DATA gap for a native kext is about 166 KiB.
    NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp d2a85cbcb4ad29df03a05c9f4e3edc0120358ab90a731cb61b083accf93bd31f -> 6c17459b67b868874f6be56b68c17155da10abd03f52efefdca79a102aed01e7
      the render server is WindowServer (kRenderServer/isRenderServer at the six "backboardd" sites, as UniXNU Adreno740 7487f72).
    NativeAdrenoPublish.h   b266fa844b199254611f2bb1fc0bfca6dedd1c73535cf442838b07527e74a854 -> 9b7f30aa11694cfb44a7731b1efc4fbe5a73ebf7807acee1443aa932fb01c46b
      macOS process lists (NativeAdrenoSandboxGrantList, NativeAdrenoLargeClientList) in place of iPadOS's.
    NativeAdrenoMemory.cpp  ea99b5e92be53377467c830bb63e5043597e543692ec20087711ba4d67770b1c -> 28882d551523a43a27890f4ed2fb82968bcbefcfdece71cf68465a9bdf6effad
      the pool's 128 KiB extent table on the heap, allocated with the pool (same __DATA reason).
  Not compiled into the kext: NativeAdrenoAccelerator.cpp (the iPadOS IOAcceleratorES class), NativeAdrenoClient.cpp and
  NativeAdrenoBoard.cpp (host-only), tests/ and scripts/ (host tools). The source lists are those of scripts/build-adreno830.py.
  NativeAdrenoABI.h (the v2 user-client ABI Turnip's darwin KMD includes) is unchanged, byte for byte.

ArmSmmu4K (github.com/UniXNU/ArmSmmu4K), 3ba92451bd44bb742d11758fbfcd3a446ecad685, MIT (kits/ArmSmmu4K/LICENSE, sha256
7a730b868c1ff986cdfc210a7b140ab4e0a31bf7db1d15db901427973efaa70f). The revision Adreno830 1a13210 was built and tested against
(its docs/PROGRESS.md: "ArmSmmu4K 3ba9245"); the local checkout's 83969cd (UniXNU's catalog pin) has a newer, incompatible
ArmSmmu4KLiveArena (per-page table allocation) and the archive's 4d0d659 lacks ArmSmmu4KLiveMapContextBatchExclusive. Taken from
GitHub's archive of that commit: the 8 sources and 8 headers, README.md and LICENSE unchanged; the kit's own tests left out.

